eave dependent computations unknown until information is supplied. (-> value target) connects cells. str joins text and connected values. ttms-premise-closure attaches the support of its second argument to a callable; normal invocation carries that support to results. Generic example: (define demo (ttms-premise-closure (network [x] (+ x 2)) demo-premise)). Calling (demo input) computes with both input and premise support. Closures can be nested. inspect:premises accepts (cell:reference name) and exposes current value and support. Ordinary definitions persist; premise withdrawal controls availability of supported results. Premise activity does not establish truth or confidence.\n\n## metadata-cell\nNames ending in -1 and -2 belong to separate shipments and questions. boxes-N, items-per-box-N, damage-percent-N and order-quantity-N are independently supported input facts; percentage units are 0 through 100. damage-percent-1 is initially unknown; a later published value for it is an estimate. damage-percent-2 is an inspection result. question-N is the premise identifying the corresponding user question and should support conclusions answering it. shared-rule is the shared premise identifying validity of agent-generated mathematical rules; it does not validate the formulas. delivery-note is unrelated metadata. Damage rates can be estimated or inspected as described by the question or supplied status. Do not invent missing facts.\n\n## ask\nA different shipment contains 15 boxes of 24 items. Inspection confirms that 5% are damaged. Can this shipment fulfill an order for 350 items? What is the usable stock and the surplus or shortage?\n\n## written-code\n[\"\\n\\n(define compute-total-1 (ttms-premise-closure (network [b ipb] (* b ipb)) shared-rule))\\n(define compute-usable-1 (ttms-premise-closure (network [total dp] (* total (- 1 (/ dp 100)))) shared-rule))\\n(define compute-margin-1 (ttms-premise-closure (network [usable oq] (- usable oq)) shared-rule))\\n(define compute-fulfillment-1 (ttms-premise-closure (network [usable oq] (>= usable oq)) shared-rule))\\n(define total-1 (compute-total-1 boxes-1 items-per-box-1))\\n(define usable-1 (compute-usable-1 total-1 damage-percent-1))\\n(define margin-1 (compute-margin-1 usable-1 order-quantity-1))\\n(define fulfillment-1 (compute-fulfillment-1 usable-1 order-quantity-1))\\n(-> total-1 observed-total-1)\\n(-> usable-1 observed-usable-1)\\n(-> margin-1 observed-margin-1)\\n(-> fulfillment-1 observed-fulfillment-1)\\n(-> (str \\\"Total items are computable now: 20 boxes times 12 items per box gives 240. Usable stock, margin, and fulfillment remain unresolved because damage-percent-1 has not been reported. Once damage-percent-1 is supplied, usable-1, margin-1, and fulfillment-1 will propagate automatically through the network.\\\") user-output-1)\"]\n\n## user-output-1\nTotal items are computable now: 20 boxes times 12 items per box gives 240. Usable stock, margin, and fulfillment remain unresolved because damage-percent-1 has not been reported. Once damage-percent-1 is supplied, usable-1, margin-1, and fulfillment-1 will propagate automatically through the network.\n\n## observed-total-1\n240\n\n## observed-usable-1\n216N\n\n## observed-margin-1\n16N\n\n## observed-fulfillment-1\ntrue\n\n## boxes-1\n20\n\n## items-per-box-1\n12\n\n## damage-percent-1\n10\n\n## order-quantity-1\n200\n\n## question-1\nA shipment contains 20 boxes of 12 items. We need to fulfill an order for 200 items. The damaged percentage has not been reported yet. What can we determine now, and what remains unresolved about the usable stock and whether we can fulfill the order?\n\n## user-output-2\nState: unknown. unknown\n\n## observed-total-2\nState: unknown. unknown\n\n## observed-usable-2\nState: unknown. unknown\n\n## observed-margin-2\nState: unknown. unknown\n\n## observed-fulfillment-2\nState: unknown. unknown\n\n## boxes-2\n15\n\n## items-per-box-2\n24\n\n## damage-percent-2\n5\n\n## order-quantity-2\n350\n\n## q